WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.337
Let’s walk through Draft actions.

00:00:02.337 --> 00:00:05.250
Translate the room’s decision into a complete action that another

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.188
reviewer can understand without oral context.

00:00:08.188 --> 00:00:11.488
Capture intent, instruments, targets, timing, expected

00:00:11.488 --> 00:00:14.650
effects, assumptions, and rationale before handoff.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.475
On this slide, create and revise your team's actions

00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:18.262
here.

00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:20.988
Once submitted, they become read-only while White

00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:22.488
Cell reviews them.

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:25.400
In practice, translate the room’s choice into a complete

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.475
action with enough evidence for the next reviewer to act

00:00:28.475 --> 00:00:28.637
.

00:00:29.135 --> 00:00:31.973
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:35.860
Strategic Orientation establishes the opening position.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.360
Move tabs keep actions attached to the correct round.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.860
Submitted or forwarded records become read-only at the documented boundary

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:43.985
.

00:00:43.985 --> 00:00:46.760
When you are ready, use Open actions to move

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.373
to the live surface.

00:00:48.373 --> 00:00:51.310
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:51.460
.
